WEBVTT

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.530
You have wonderful eyes.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:51.410
They look like fish eyes. I like them.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:54.250
Those cold, emotionless eyes.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.690
Everyone knows about you.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:00.620
A father, one child...

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:03.730
One of them killed the other.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.790
He killed my mother.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.190
That's why I killed him.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.930
In other words, you have no place to go
nor a place to go back to.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.540
Why don't you come with us?

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:19.840
With?

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:22.540
If you'll follow us, I'll give you a job.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.510
A job suited for those eyes of yours.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:48.130
<i>Norikonda sabaibaru cousutaa</i>

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:48.100
The survival roller coaster we got on

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.870
There's no need to give up,
run by the highway

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:50.570
<i>Akirame muyoude run by the highway</i>

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.440
<i>Kimiwa inochi karagara</i>

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:52.640
You just barely escaped with your life

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.970
<i>Atashitachimo nodoga karakara</i>

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:55.240
We're thirsty

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:57.170
<i>Kyokugento mugendai</i>

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.380
Extremities and infinity

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.510
<i>Tomo ni sorette mugendai</i>

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.740
Together, they form a fantasy

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:01.410
<i>Kamaeta me hibana chiri</i>

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:01.610
The eyes, squaring away, are
throwing out sparks

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:04.440
<i>Oni-san kochira to shita o dasu</i>

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:04.670
"You're it! This way, " you say,
as you stick your tongue out

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:06.670
<i>Wink</i>

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:06.740
Wink

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.350
<i>Kyouretsuna itamini kansha</i>

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:10.560
Grateful for the excruciating pain

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.690
<i>Power to iu na no rei de henkan</i>

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.990
I'm restored by a gratitude
known as power

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:18.600
<i>Mou sorosoro okaeri asobareta houga
iinodewa naide shouka</i>

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:18.800
Perhaps it would be better too return soon?

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:27.500
<i>Matsugeno sukima umeruyouni aimeiku</i>

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:27.740
As though filling in the gaps between
the eyelashes, eye make

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:34.810
<i>Kokorono sukima umeruyouni I take</i>

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:35.010
As though filling in the gaps of
my heart, I take

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:39.280
<i>Gekiretsu panchide gyakuni takamaru</i>

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:39.480
On the contrary, the intensity is heightened
by a powerful punch

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.750
<i>Yabai shiuchi hodo yokei moechauwa</i>

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:43.820
The worse I'm treated, the more I get fired up

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:48.120
<i>Mouretsu panchide atashi takaburu</i>

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:48.260
I get worked up over an intense punch

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:56.550
<i>Sonna koto shite kurete arigatou</i>

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:57.100
Thank you for doing such a thing

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:59.070
<i>Sukima sukima sukimani mimai</i>

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.270
A gap, a gap, pay a sympathy visit

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.070
<i>Janai janai itainjanai?</i>

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:01.240
Doesn't it, doesn't it, doesn't it hurt?

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.740
<i>Mimai tsurai? ltai? Yabai?</i>

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.010
Is the visit painful? Does it hurt?
Is it dangerous?

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:07.370
<i>lkitai itai shitai, lkitai itai shitai</i>

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:07.680
I want to go, I want to stay, I want to do it

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:15.120
Just sticking your arms out isn't any good!
Put your back into it!

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.160
Okay!

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:23.330
<i>Shell of Origin</i>

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.390
Good, good.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:21.500
I thought you wouldn't be any good
at things like this,

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.590
but you've actually got
quite a knack for it, Asami.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:27.360
Do your best, Asami.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.200
Yes, Sir.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:33.710
Becoming strong is good, but don't
make your personality take after her.

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:36.110
Hey, Baldy, what the hell does that mean?

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.380
You said it! You said it!

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:40.970
What I mean is, I want her to become someone
who won't talk in such a vulgar manner!

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:45.380
Where are you going?

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.960
Off to eat udon noodles.
Do I have good taste, or what?

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:50.550
Hey, I'll go too!

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:52.930
Asami, we'll continue this later.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.400
Okay.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:05.110
For whatever reason, Mikura's sticking
real close to Mr. Kurokawa recently.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:06.470
Mr. Harada...

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:15.050
Compared to how you were at the beginning,
you've changed quite a bit, Asami.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:22.960
I want to become strong. Like you, Miss Mikura!

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:26.130
If you're weak of heart, you won't live
long enough to eat dinner. Got it?

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:29.120
I'm going to become strong.
And then, someday...

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:33.130
I'm telling you, I don't need a bodyguard.

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:36.270
But it's been really dangerous lately!

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:37.770
I can't say it clearly,

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:40.080
but now, there's something different
from what's been going on so far.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.280
Well, when that happens, it happens.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:45.480
What time is it now? Now's the time to eat.
Time to eat udon noodles.

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:46.710
Yeesh...

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.190
When it comes time to pay the bill,
I pay half, you pay half.

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:51.450
Whoa, cheapskate!

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:00.590
What's with you, all of a sudden?

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.860
I want to protect you. That's all.

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.830
While I'm grateful, that's still...

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:13.110
You, Harada, Asami...

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:15.300
I definitely won't let my friends die.

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:16.870
Mikura...

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:19.870
Pops!

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:52.280
Yeah, he opened fire out of the blue.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.770
We'll run as much as we can,
but I'm counting on you.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:00.320
Stop it. Against a guy with a submachine gun,
the odds aren't in your favor.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:02.590
But we need to finish him off here!

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:13.860
Something's not right.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.820
Pops!

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:33.880
Once in a while...

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:48.400
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.300
Thank you.

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.810
I thought I'd die this time
and cross the river Styx.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.180
I told you it was dangerous!

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:04.780
But normally, you wouldn't expect someone
to come from the front door.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:15.530
<i>Mugi-ya</i>

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:15.530
I see. He couldn't fire.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.800
He clearly hesitated in opening fire.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.200
Not toward Kurokawa, but I'm afraid...

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.430
DSA's lone female?

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:28.240
Probably, though I don't think he's concerned
about dragging other people into this.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.510
So does that mean he's a boy after all?

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:34.210
Well, what shall we do?

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:38.890
Curve your toes upward!

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:39.820
Okay!

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:43.660
Securely plant your pivot foot and kick like
it's going through something!

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:44.630
Okay!

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.650
Hey! Doing good!

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:51.320
What's the matter?

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:56.940
I'm still not the same as everyone else here.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:58.540
In what way?

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:02.510
Well, Mr. Kurokawa's life being
threatened all this time...

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:05.140
No one even mentioned such
an important thing to me.

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:07.780
He's not concerned about it,

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:09.650
so there wasn't a reason to mention it either.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:13.490
There's got to be something I can do to help too.

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:15.890
Your thoughts are enough.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.330
Say, Asami.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.230
Yes?

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:21.320
You won't be any good so long as you're
thinking you want to be useful to us.

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:24.830
What you do for yourself
is what you do for everyone.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:26.700
What you do for everyone
is what you do for yourself.

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:29.130
That's what friends are like.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:34.180
Hey, Pops! I told you not to come out.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:37.200
Well, that's why I'd like you to do
some shopping for me.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.180
There's a new Go-ya Noodle on sale.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:41.750
It should be at the local
convenience store, so let's go!

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:42.720
Then I'll...

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:45.450
No, it's okay. You continue your training.

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:47.090
Okay.

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:49.820
Rubber noodles, right? I'm on my way.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:52.060
Not rubber! Go-ya!
I can't take this anymore. Go-ya!

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:54.320
I got it, I got it.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:58.560
Yeesh, just how long do I need to stay like this?

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:01.500
Well, in her place...

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:02.700
I may look like this, but...

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:04.100
I'll be all right.

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:06.600
Oh, man.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:11.910
What kind of noodles were they?
Well, I'll know when I get there.

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:16.750
Don't let your guard down.
That girl's like a bomb.

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:23.120
There weren't any sesame noodles.

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:29.700
What? Go-ya? Is there really such a thing?

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:32.000
Well, I'll look for it one more time.

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:36.290
What is it?

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:39.170
So what do you want?

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:41.710
I'm in the middle of shopping.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:43.770
Come along with us quietly.

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:57.620
What's the meaning of this?

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.750
What the hell were you guys think...

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:03.820
All right, take her.

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:09.470
Damn! Couldn't have been helped.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.930
Isn't Mikura a little late?

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:18.070
Maybe she stopped somewhere
on her way back?

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:21.240
Good work out there.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:24.420
Miss Mikura's late.

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:28.050
Yeah, she should have come home ages ago.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:29.950
That's weird.

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:31.160
What's the matter?

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:33.220
I can't get through to her.

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:36.460
<i>Closed Today</i>

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:41.270
What the hell is this? Hey!

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:44.640
Scissor-scissor macho, tell me
what the hell's the deal here!

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:49.300
I'm sorry. Please remain calm
for just a little while longer.

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:53.820
I said, tell me what the hell is going on!

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:56.810
This is only until a certain person's
job is finished.

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:59.420
Oh, would you like something to drink?

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:02.150
Job? What's with that?

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:09.660
What kind of people were they?

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:17.130
She met some weird gang at the front
of the store and went somewhere.

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:21.080
Meaning, I get the feeling
something's happened.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:24.810
Being a couch potato at home isn't acceptable.
I think it's deplorable.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:28.480
Damn!

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.120
I'm going to the police for a bit.

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:34.360
If you find out anything,
give me a call right away.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:38.190
Roger. You be careful too, Mr. Kurokawa.

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:41.330
What should I...

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:44.860
Sorry, Asami. Could you stay put at the agency?

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:47.560
There might be a call coming in there.

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:49.460
Yes.

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:53.270
I'm going to take another look around
this area. Counting on you.

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:58.350
It's me.

00:11:58.350 --> 00:11:59.810
What do you want?

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:03.650
I fixed it so your job will go smoothly.

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:05.820
What's that supposed to mean?

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:08.880
Continue without hesitation.
Kurokawa's currently...

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:15.550
There's no need to abruptly hang up.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:20.800
I keep telling you, don't interfere with my work.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:24.510
I figured there had to be a reason a skilled man,
someone the boss himself raised under his care,

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.800
let things drag on this long.

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:28.900
What are you trying to say?

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.810
Did you fall in love with that girl?

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:36.540
Of all things, that Fish-Eyes Kazuto fell
for DSA's orange girl...

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:41.220
I wouldn't... Enough of your nonsense!

00:12:57.240 --> 00:12:59.810
At times like this, I lose my voice.

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:02.440
Really? They're no different from
what they always are.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:04.270
Your cute voice, your face...

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:08.250
Oh, Chief! Say, say!

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:11.510
Take me out to that really great
grilled beef place next time.

00:13:12.050 --> 00:13:15.890
Lately, I've been so busy, it's hard...

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:15.090
<i>The taste of youth. Bocky!</i>

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:15.890
<i>The Taste of Youth
Standing Aroma,
the Taste of Youth</i>

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:19.060
Give me a moment.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:22.430
Yeesh! You change the subject just like that.

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:26.430
Kurokawa?! I'm in the middle of something.
Tell him to come later!

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:27.800
Who was that?

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:29.570
Just some ridiculous guy.

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:33.370
It's already been two years since
I began coming here.

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:35.080
Yeah...

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:37.750
<i>Welcome! Glittering Lips Aya-chan</i>

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.250
<i>Police Chief for a Day</i>

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:40.820
Pleased to meet you!

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:43.380
My daughter has much to be thankful to you for.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:44.480
For real?

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:49.490
I was surprised to find out
you were Mitsuko's father.

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:54.120
I did hear from her about her father
being a police chief.

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:57.270
She always talked about you.

00:13:57.270 --> 00:14:00.070
But you're such a bad man, Chief.

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:02.730
Laying hands on your daughter's friend...

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:06.170
Though you're the one who asked me out.

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:07.730
Is that right?

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:12.110
How long can we keep doing this?

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:15.950
If we're discovered, you, me, we'll both...

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:19.390
It's all right. There's nothing to worry about.

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:21.490
What?

00:14:21.490 --> 00:14:23.010
It's a little rowdy out there.

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:26.760
What the...

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:27.690
Hide!

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:32.400
Stop it! We'll arrest you for committing a public
disturbance in front of police officers!

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:34.540
You're the ones causing a disturbance.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:35.940
This'll be settled quickly.

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:38.530
You... What's the meaning of this?

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:40.970
Don't tell me that he knows!

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:43.240
Sorry to disturb you out of the blue,

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:45.250
but could you give me everything you've got?

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:46.540
Everything, you say?

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:50.440
A friend of mine is in a bit of trouble
and I don't have much time.

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:52.520
What happened?

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:55.090
I don't have the time to explain, or come to think
of it, money in any shape or form either.

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:56.660
But right out of the blue!

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:59.180
You don't care if this is the last date
you have with that girl?

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:03.530
Sorry for dropping in on you and
causing all the other disturbance.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:06.800
Stay back!

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.370
But, Chief!

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:12.540
There's no need to worry! Just don't come in
until I give you my approval!

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:13.770
Right. Right. That's exactly right.
Yes, Sir!

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:16.310
That's all I have for now.

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:19.810
I'm always rooting for you when
you're on TV, Glittering Lips.

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:21.320
Does that sound too much like a cliché?

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:22.480
Thanks.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.550
Oh, she doesn't like me?

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:26.290
Leave already!

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:29.660
I'm worried sick over how I'm going to
sweep this disturbance under the rug!

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:31.830
How about telling them a friend of yours
who came to borrow money from you?

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.390
Pull yourself together.

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:34.990
Yeah, I'll do that.

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:40.260
What's with him? More than that,
how does he know about us?

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:43.570
There's no need for you to worry about it.

00:15:43.570 --> 00:15:45.810
I've already taken steps to take care of him.

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:48.500
I'm not in the mood anymore. I'm going home.

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:50.510
Aya...

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:56.310
Damn! Now I can't just leave things
up to the barber!

00:15:56.880 --> 00:15:58.880
Don't jerk me around, Kurokawa!

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:02.690
Whoa, it's amazing he gave you all this.

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:05.090
I had to use harsh methods
in order to get my way.

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:08.990
Well, now isn't the time to worry about that.
So, any leads?

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:10.730
None.

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:12.560
That's worrying.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:16.640
First of all, we don't know why
Mikura was targeted.

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:17.970
I wonder if that's it?

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:19.470
That?

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:22.310
To make me easier to kill.

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:25.580
Meaning, removing the bodyguard first?

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:28.650
While the work of a bodyguard is full of tension,

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:33.550
when you're alone and off duty,
you let your guard down quite a bit.

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:37.860
In this case, we're the ones who'll
have to make the move.

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:39.160
You're right.

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:50.840
No way! But is she all right?

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:53.430
Right now, he's the only lead we have.

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:56.000
If anything happens, contact us immediately.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:59.340
Mr. Harada!

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:11.230
What you do for yourself is
what you do for everyone.

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:13.360
What you do for everyone is
what you do for yourself.

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:15.090
That's what friends are like.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.430
I have to go too!

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:28.930
It really is Miss Mikura's!

00:17:30.310 --> 00:17:32.940
<i>Mugi-ya
Closed Today</i>

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:35.380
You're that killer's...

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:38.750
He's my prized hunter.

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:41.090
If you're around, you get a little bit in the way.

00:17:41.090 --> 00:17:44.430
Why? You got some grudge against Pops?

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:47.290
Well, I can't say you don't have
any grudges against him at all.

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:49.290
It's just a job.

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:51.820
So there's a client.

00:17:52.930 --> 00:17:54.420
It's a job.

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:00.930
No way!

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:04.530
They won't make it in time!

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:06.250
Wait!

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:08.120
While you're here...

00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:10.310
I have to save her!

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:19.590
Asami?

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:26.330
What a brave little girl!

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:27.800
Did you come to rescue her?

00:18:27.800 --> 00:18:28.970
Curve toes upward,

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:31.560
securely plant the pivot foot and kick
like it's going through something.

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:32.610
Kick!

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:40.300
Asami!

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:42.680
Miss Mikura!

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:48.960
I was just going to give you a shave,
since you were here...

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.060
That's none of your business!

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:52.080
I'm sorry.

00:18:56.430 --> 00:18:58.730
This certainly isn't a good feeling.

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:00.790
Acting like ground bait for when
one goes fishing, that is.

00:19:56.790 --> 00:20:00.690
You fell for it, Mr. Handsome Boy Assassin!

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:05.960
Drop your gun!

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:09.500
Who hired you?

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:13.500
If you don't cooperate and give me the answer,
I'll send you to the afterlife.

00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:17.910
You've been hitting me hard quite a bit,
so I'm being serious.

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:20.010
Where's Mikura?

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:21.980
If you won't answer, I'll just...

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:25.820
I fixed it so your job will go smoothly.

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:28.150
It's got nothing to do with me.

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:30.220
Don't play dumb!

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:39.030
Harada!

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:41.030
Run, Mr. Kurokawa!

00:21:00.390 --> 00:21:03.520
Well, looks like my back's to the wall.

00:21:03.520 --> 00:21:05.290
You, you, you.

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:09.560
Since this is it, could you at least
tell me who hired you?

00:21:15.070 --> 00:21:15.900
What?

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:23.210
Mikura, what were you doing all this time?

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:26.380
I was in a bind, but Asami rescued me.

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:28.810
I was held captive by the scissor-scissor macho.

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:31.720
Mugiyama...

00:21:32.320 --> 00:21:35.250
I couldn't get a hold of you on your cell,
so I came directly.

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:38.520
If it's Mugiyama, then could it be...

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:40.490
Pops?

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:44.020
Why, you!

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:47.060
Mikura, you idiot!

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:02.750
Oh, no!

00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:18.800
Mr. Kurokawa, are you all right?

00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:20.100
Well, at least I am.

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:23.100
What is that supposed to mean?

00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:26.100
I'll have to check out the meaning of it now.

00:22:26.870 --> 00:22:29.140
Did something happen over there?

00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:31.010
Well...

00:22:31.010 --> 00:22:35.150
An assassination group that accepts contracts
on people's lives has been discovered.

00:22:35.150 --> 00:22:38.990
The Metropolitan Police Department
has put out a country-wide APB

00:22:38.990 --> 00:22:44.460
for the arrest of the Black Scissors
and a part of its group, the DSA.

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:45.830
These three people are it.

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:47.730
<i>Culprit Group on the Run</i>

00:22:46.590 --> 00:22:47.730
No way.

00:22:54.670 --> 00:22:58.700
We've moved in on the Black Scissors.
Next is the DSA.

00:22:59.510 --> 00:23:01.240
What's the meaning of this?!

00:23:01.240 --> 00:23:02.570
Understood.

00:23:04.880 --> 00:23:06.310
This is a great opportunity.

00:23:06.450 --> 00:23:08.940
I'll squeeze out all the pus in this city at once!

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:10.250
<i>Shell of Origin</i>

00:23:15.560 --> 00:23:20.730
